<title>CHINA: China seen importing 1.5 mln tonnes of barley.</title>
<headline>China seen importing 1.5 mln tonnes of barley.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's barley imports were estimated at 1.5 million tonnes in 1996/97, the Economic Information News said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Domestic barley output would remain steady at 4.0 million tonnes this year, unchanged from 1996, while demand was expected to be 5.5 million tonnes, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>Imports of barley reached 1.41 million tonnes in 1995/96, up 118 percent over the 1994/95 peroid, it said without elaborating further on the dates.</p>
<p>Output of sorghum was estimated at 5.0 million tonnes in 1996/97 compared with demand of 4.95 million tonnes, the newspaper said without giving further details.</p>
<p>--Beijing Newsroom (8610) 64532 1921</p>
</text>
